Subject: [PATCH 237/260] [ae-patch] Fix the review findings on the bypass
 relaunch switch

Every claude-native permission change now pins the target in the launch args and gets the long forward budget, so a stale label can no longer relaunch Plan back into bypass. The runner relaunches when the pane mode is unknown, bounds the whole restart at 70 s, and reads the new mode inside the switching lock. The server restores the old args only after a definite refusal or an unreached runner; an unknown outcome keeps whichever pin does not ask for bypass and leaves the label alone. A restart whose mode could not be read keeps the pin and stamps no label. wait_while_switching now waits through queued relaunches. The composer names the mode Claude is in when it differs from the request.
